    "methods_description": "Each session included 25 lists structured as encoding, distractor, and cued recall phases. During encoding, 6 word pairs were presented sequentially for 4000 ms each with a 1000 ms interstimulus interval. During cued recall, one word from each pair was shown and participants had 5000 ms to vocally recall the paired word. iEEG recordings were collected using monopolar and bipolar referencing schemes across multiple recording systems, with voltage values scaled to a common unit (V), and electrode locations annotated with MNI/Talairach coordinates and brain region labels.",
